  "rules": [
    "Status is dot and word in a table cell, and a chip in a record, card and board.",
    "A value with options never renders as free text. If it has an option set, it gets an Option or Options part.",
    "Numbers align right and use tabular figures in every cell and record row.",
    "Money always knows its currency. Cents show in record and form; cells may round to whole units only when every row in the column does.",
    "The field overrides the grid, the grid overrides the surface. A field may name a variant (display: { cell: \"chip\" }); a surface never can.",
    "Editable is the same part with a chevron or a control, never a different-looking part. Read and edit share size, colour and position.",
    "Empty is a muted em dash, never a blank cell or null.",
    "An ordinal set sorts by its order, never the alphabet, and draws its tones as a ramp in that order. Status tones are for states only.",
    "Option sets are data: a field points at its set (devops.option_sets, published as schema/option-sets.json). A status option's tone is its state's: done lime, moving sky, waiting amber, failed rose, ended neutral.",
    "Every value has a text form, the plain string for CSV export, aria-label, copy and search. A secret has none, export included."
  ]
}
